  "slug": "coding-rnas-generates-6c5b",
  "summary": "Six items build reproducible workflows, curated resources and portals for spatial and single-cell data, from HuBMAP's 9,316 datasets to traceable curation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is infrastructure for harmonizing, curating and reusing spatial and single-cell data rather than new inference methods. The HuBMAP Data Portal hosts 9,316 public datasets from healthy human tissues with search and visualization tools. SpaceBlocks supplies a Snakemake workflow for expert-supervised cohort-level spatial transcriptomics. TRACE emphasizes traceable curation of public omics data, demonstrated in a harmonised single-cell glaucoma resource. NLM-CKN links cell phenotypes from 88 datasets and 10 organs to Cell Ontology, genes, diseases and drugs. SENgEAR offers a no-code platform for comparing senescence signatures and cell-cell communication. QUEST, which virtually stains H&E to predict multiplex immunofluorescence protein expression, is a modeling contribution adjacent to this thread, linking histology to spatial proteomics.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-08"
}
